THOUGHT: I need to prevent a @Nullable ShaderProgram from being passed to the @NonNull overload. The simplest fix is to add an explicit null check in the 4-arg render method and throw a GdxRuntimeException if shader is null, matching existing error-handling style. Then I should run the compile task to confirm the NullAway error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '710,712c\  public void render(@Nullable ShaderProgram shader, int primitiveType, int offset, int count) {
    if (shader == null) {
      throw new GdxRuntimeException("shader must not be null");
    }
    render(shader, primitiveType, offset, count, autoBind);
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/Mesh.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "PASS_NULLABLE" new_build_output.log | head && tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

